Title: Senior QA Engineer
Years of experience: 6
English level: intermediate

More than 10 years of experience in trade. Has experience in managing the department. Since 2017, I switched to testing and do not stop there, I strive to become better and more professional.
I am a Senior QA Engineer with experience testing mobile and web applications in retail management system, cloud and local infrastructure platforms, database management tools, highly loaded distributed systems.

I have good skills in System Testing, including Functional Testing, Performance Testing, Scalability Testing, Reliability Testing, Configuration Testing, and Security Testing. I also have extensive experience working with databases such as MySQL, Oracle, and MSSQL, PostgreSQL.

- 6 years experience in Software Testing and Quality Assurance;
- Training new employees (mentoring/development of individual development plans for Intern/Junior QAs);
- Organization of test process, ensuring control and creating of test reports;
- Creating test design, reviewing and preparing test artifacts: checklists, test cases, bug reports, test summary reports, test data preparation;
- Testing of client-server web applications (GUI and integration testing, regression), mobile. Cooperation with developers, analysts, technical support and managers;
- Experience in Web and mobile (iOS, android) application testing;
- Audit technical documentation;
- Analyzing and solving end-user’s problem reports;
- Understanding of the software development cycle, methodologies and testing methodologies;
- Understanding of Agile principles.

Operating Systems: Mac OS, Windows, iOS, Android, Linux.
Ticket systems: Jira, Trello, Mantis.
Test Management Systems: TestRail, TestLink.
Technologies and Tools: CI/CD, SQL, Postman, Fiddler, Chrome DevTools, Git, Visual Studio Code, Charles, Fiddler, iTools, iTunes, Testflight, Kibana, Grafana.
My goal is to get a full-time position as a Senior QA Engineer in a testing team in a stable company that provides opportunities for continuous professional growth.

